.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Signals are sent to the child\(cqs \f[B]process group\f[R] (negative
PID), so all processes in the PTY session receive the signal, not just
the shell itself.
.IP \(bu 2
For window size changes, use \f[CR]bc_pty_resize(3)\f[R] instead of
sending \f[CR]SIGWINCH\f[R] manually, as \f[CR]bc_pty_resize\f[R] also
updates the terminal dimensions via \f[CR]TIOCSWINSZ\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
Signal names are matched case\-sensitively.
\f[CR]\(dqsigint\(dq\f[R] is not recognized; use
\f[CR]\(dqSIGINT\(dq\f[R] or \f[CR]\(dqINT\(dq\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
The signal is delivered synchronously on the server side before the
acknowledgement is sent.
When this function returns \f[CR]BC_OK\f[R], the \f[CR]kill(2)\f[R] call
has already completed.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]SIGKILL\f[R] and \f[CR]SIGSTOP\f[R] cannot be caught or ignored by
the child.
\f[CR]SIGKILL\f[R] will always terminate the process; \f[CR]SIGSTOP\f[R]
will always suspend it.
